81250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1381260#post1381260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it was never mentioned, and it should stay that way, for both MtA and VtM's sake</div> </div> </div> </div>what makes you say that???<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3148-zennis","name":"Zennis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T05:53:16-07:00","id":1464248,"title":"","content":"<br /> I just skimmed through it a long time ago, but I recall it has very prohibitive and unjustified rules for Ghoul Mages and Revenant Mages, stating they stop being Mages after around a decade. Apparently Vitae Gilguls a Mage according to the book. All the while there is a Tytalan Klaus Hortemone right in the Traditions' stronghold of Doissetep, content with being a Ghoul Mage, hoping to &quot;<i>one day reunite the Tremere with the Order of Hermes</i>&quot; , and being fulfilled as a person.<br /> <br /> And it has this puzzling part saying &quot;Assuming there are 10 Revenant Mages, 7 join the Nephandi.&quot;...seriously, how and why? Do the Nephandi just mysteriously show up at the doorstep of a Revenant estate a few days after a Revenant Awakens? Hogwarts style ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I can understand the Nephandi being able to do this to Widderslaintes because of shared nephandic affinity...But also snatching up Revenant Mages? Seems far-fetched, but it would not be the first time the writers give the Nephandi some very impressive and distinct capabilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-17-2021, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T10:41:11-07:00","id":1464268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464248#post1464248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it has this puzzling part saying &quot;Assuming there are 10 Revenant Mages, 7 join the Nephandi.&quot;...seriously, how and why? Do the Nephandi just mysteriously show up at the doorstep of a Revenant estate a few days after a Revenant Awakens? Hogwarts style ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I can understand the Nephandi being able to do this to Widderslaintes because of shared nephandic affinity...But also snatching up Revenant Mages? Seems far-fetched, but it would not be the first time the writers give the Nephandi some very impressive and distinct capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be the fact that Revenants generally tend towards monstrosity without being Mages. They're described as having a lesser Beast and often being violent and deranged. The majority becoming full-blown Nephandi is maybe a bit of a stretch, but half wouldn't surprise me in the least. It's not about the Nephandi swooping down on innocent little Revenant Mage children, but rather the natural tendencies of Revenants leading them in that direction. Arguably, the Curse of Caine might ping whatever they might detect in widderslaintes, but I had always thought widderslaintes just inevitably made their way back to the Nephandi on their own, not that they were actively recruited on a large scale, for much the same reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T12:16:40-07:00","id":1464274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464248#post1464248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And it has this puzzling part saying &quot;Assuming there are 10 Revenant Mages, 7 join the Nephandi.&quot;...seriously, how and why? Do the Nephandi just mysteriously show up at the doorstep of a Revenant estate a few days after a Revenant Awakens? Hogwarts style ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I can understand the Nephandi being able to do this to Widderslaintes because of shared nephandic affinity...But also snatching up Revenant Mages? Seems far-fetched, but it would not be the first time the writers give the Nephandi some very impressive and distinct capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revenents as a rule are supremely fucked up imagine the Adams family minus the funny mixed with texas chainsaw massacre and wrong turn. By the time you're awaken you'll have seen and done things which will have left their mark. Especially if your magical theory is grounded in tzmisce koldunic sorcerers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T14:13:21-07:00","id":1464279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464274#post1464274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenents as a rule are supremely fucked up imagine the Adams family minus the funny mixed with texas chainsaw massacre and wrong turn. By the time you're awaken you'll have seen and done things which will have left their mark. Especially if your magical theory is grounded in tzmisce koldunic sorcerers</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. I think some people forget sometimes that revenants are not just ghouls who produce their own vitae; they are members of inbred blood cults who have almost zero contact with the outside world. They are f-ed up in the head sufficiently that they can actually follow paths of enlightenment instead of humanity and their in-built paradigm is basically a mix of \u201cbastards of those cursed by God\u201d and \u201cwe\u2019ve made pacts with Earthbound demons.\u201d<br /> <br /> The rest of the Revised quote was that after those seven naturally fall to the Nephandi, two more just have bad luck (paradox backlash, werewolf notices them, Technocracy notices them, etc.) and that leaves, at most one still living non-Nephandi Revenant who might make it a few decades before meeting the same fate as the other two in the entire world\u2026 and you don\u2019t get to play them.<br /> <br /> Personally, I just prefer the Dhampir explanation\u2026 your soul is awakened by its nature (which is why you don\u2019t count as a sleeper), but in a different way than leads to wielding sphere magick. Revenants seem damned similar in the respect that they\u2019re conceived and born already a supernatural entity (vs. a ghoul who becomes one later).<br /> <br /> I also don\u2019t particularly mind the restriction on ghoul mages because it does make some metaphysical sense; becoming a vampire warps your avatar into something incapable of magick and you\u2019re basically drinking the same poison in a smaller dose and, as been established, long duration ghouls become more vampire-like (larger blood pools, ability to take half-damage from bashing, picking up extra flaws like sensitivity to sunlight, etc.).<br /> <br /> So while I think you could argue that Revised makes it happen too quickly, the idea that imbibing supernatural poison known to warp/destroy avatars will have no long term effects feels equally as ungrounded to me.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would have it chew through the Avatar background over time like Revised has it because your avatar is basically addicted and lazily allowing Vitae to do the work it\u2019s supposed to do in fueling magic, right down to zero where it\u2019s basically comatose, but you\u2019d retain your current Arete (increasing it would be a bitch) and ability to work sphere magick (and could even learn more spheres)\u2026 but you\u2019d need to spend blood points on it because your avatar is too drugged out to fuel the effect itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T03:55:52-07:00","id":1464351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464248#post1464248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just skimmed through it a long time ago, but I recall it has very prohibitive and unjustified rules for Ghoul Mages and Revenant Mages, stating they stop being Mages after around a decade. Apparently Vitae Gilguls a Mage according to the book. All the while there is a Tytalan Klaus Hortemone right in the Traditions' stronghold of Doissetep, content with being a Ghoul Mage, hoping to &quot;<i>one day reunite the Tremere with the Order of Hermes</i>&quot; , and being fulfilled as a person.<br /> <br /> And it has this puzzling part saying &quot;Assuming there are 10 Revenant Mages, 7 join the Nephandi.&quot;...seriously, how and why? Do the Nephandi just mysteriously show up at the doorstep of a Revenant estate a few days after a Revenant Awakens? Hogwarts style ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I can understand the Nephandi being able to do this to Widderslaintes because of shared nephandic affinity...But also snatching up Revenant Mages? Seems far-fetched, but it would not be the first time the writers give the Nephandi some very impressive and distinct capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a very silly Gygaxian &quot;no fun allowed&quot; rant in that book. Being a revenant mage (or worse - ghoul mage) is <i>far</i> from the powergaming choice when it comes to MtA. Not the worst thing you could do with your freebies, but not the best either. But misters Cohen and DiPessa seemed to think that it's something all the nasty minmaxers would drool over. Really strange, and I hope outdated, mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T05:34:00-07:00","id":1464366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464279#post1464279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much this. I think some people forget sometimes that revenants are not just ghouls who produce their own vitae; they are members of inbred blood cults who have almost zero contact with the outside world. They are f-ed up in the head sufficiently that they can actually follow paths of enlightenment instead of humanity and their in-built paradigm is basically a mix of \u201cbastards of those cursed by God\u201d and \u201cwe\u2019ve made pacts with Earthbound demons.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, that's exactly why I would say they shouldn't just become Nephandi, in a similar way as being from the Sabbat probably means you're a monster but doesn't make you a Baali.<br /> <br /> They already have their own brand of evil that probably doesn't revolve arround returning creation to the primeval void for it's own good, nor releasing the demon lords from their chains (that one could be closer, but most Tzimisce wouldn't aprove that kind of talk), last time I saw their idea of trascendence was about becoming a &quot;superior predator&quot; or something like that. As you say, blood cults.<br /> <br /> But then, Mage doesn't talk much about evil mages outside Nephandi and that whole section it's rather poor (clearly just meant to discourage the idea), so one can't expect much. I wouldn't read much onto that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-18-2021, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:00:11-07:00","id":1464372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464366#post1464366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ironically, that's exactly why I would say they shouldn't just become Nephandi, in a similar way as being from the Sabbat probably means you're a monster but doesn't make you a Baali.<br /> <br /> They already have their own brand of evil that probably doesn't revolve arround returning creation to the primeval void for it's own good, nor releasing the demon lords from their chains (that one could be closer, but most Tzimisce wouldn't aprove that kind of talk), last time I saw their idea of trascendence was about becoming a &amp;quot;superior predator&amp;quot; or something like that. As you say, blood cults.<br /> <br /> But then, Mage doesn't talk much about evil mages outside Nephandi and that whole section it's rather poor (clearly just meant to discourage the idea), so one can't expect much. I wouldn't read much onto that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and like I said, I much prefer the V20/M20 approach that Dhampirs and Revenants (or any other \u2018Nightfolk\u2019 by birth) never become Mages because their souls/avatars are already awakened in a manner incompatible with sphere magick (or any other innatr supernatural type; ex. Werewolves or Changelings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T07:58:15-07:00","id":1464382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464351#post1464351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a very silly Gygaxian &quot;no fun allowed&quot; rant in that book. Being a revenant mage (or worse - ghoul mage) is <i>far</i> from the powergaming choice when it comes to MtA. Not the worst thing you could do with your freebies, but not the best either. But misters Cohen and DiPessa seemed to think that it's something all the nasty minmaxers would drool over. Really strange, and I hope outdated, mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that part of the book was ridiculous. Not only did it completely dismiss the desire to play a revenant mage as power gaming and minmaxing, but even worse it advised Storytellers to use passive aggressive rule bending to torment players who make character design choices that they disagree with rather than just talking to them about it and saying that they don't think they should make such a character. It actually is a toxic attitude that has troubled role playing as a hobby going back to original D&amp;D - that instead of talking about problematic issues out of game like adults, that DMs (or STs or whatever) should just break rules and use their power to punish players for doing things that they don't like.<br /> <br /> Really, assuming you're playing a Mage game, being a revenant is an advantage, but hardly an unbalancing one especially when you consider freebie point costs. Going back to the D&amp;D analogy, if you want to play a wizard that uses a sword and wears light armor, that can be advantageous, but considering the other powers that wizards have, is really quite minor - especially when there are other wizards in the party who used their feats to enhance their magical abilities instead. Being a revenant mage is a thematic choice, someone wants to do it because its cool, not because the boost to physical resilience and a point or two of Disciplines is that unbalancing for a game with sphere magic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T12:20:12-07:00","id":1464400,"title":"","content":"I will say mechanically a revenent mage would be a paper tiger anyway You're wasting xp if you're spending it on disciplines instead of spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-19-2021, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T16:35:58-07:00","id":1464432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zennis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire#post1381250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">seriously, was the events in this book ever even mentioned in the vampire timeline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being it's a Year of Revelations title, crossover title, Week of Nightmares sequel-ish title, and full of goofball rules, it kind of hits all checkmarks for the &quot;let's pretend it doesn't exist&quot; end of WW rulebook quality.<br /> <br /> Avatar Storm wallops the Order of Hermes. Tytalans turn to vitae as a power source and get more than they bargained for, and decide instead of doing anything intelligent, they'll wag the dog and drag the Order into a &quot;war&quot; they're not really interested in waging...<i>again</i>. Because it's House Tytalus.<br /> <br /> Hermetics raid some chantries and cheese off an Inner Councilor, who then snitches to the Order the Tytalans are just high on their own supply. Situation gets defused when the rest of the Order tells the Tytalans to fuck off and clean up their own mess. Literally nobody else cares, except <i>maybe</i> some Tzimisce with Hermetic hookups and a vested interest in Tremere misery.<br /> <br /> Considering everything else that was going on during that part of the metaplot, it's a tempest in a teakettle and barely a footnote in either supernaturals' histories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T10:46:46-07:00","id":1464522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464351#post1464351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a very silly Gygaxian &quot;no fun allowed&quot; rant in that book. Being a revenant mage (or worse - ghoul mage) is <i>far</i> from the powergaming choice when it comes to MtA. Not the worst thing you could do with your freebies, but not the best either. But misters Cohen and DiPessa seemed to think that it's something all the nasty minmaxers would drool over. Really strange, and I hope outdated, mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464279#post1464279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much this. I think some people forget sometimes that revenants are not just ghouls who produce their own vitae; they are members of inbred blood cults who have almost zero contact with the outside world. They are f-ed up in the head sufficiently that they can actually follow paths of enlightenment instead of humanity and their in-built paradigm is basically a mix of \u201cbastards of those cursed by God\u201d and \u201cwe\u2019ve made pacts with Earthbound demons.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>But this is so dark, and bleak even for WoD. A Revenant who becomes a Mage gets an Essence, her Avatar, some starting Spheres, mystical Backgrounds...She might have very dark inclinations because of who she is and being part of a Revenant family, but still, I think she <a href=\"https://ibb.co/album/pfbS8v\" target=\"_blank\">has a shot of going in this direction</a>. Maybe joining the Traditions, maybe becoming a better person, maybe rising to be some insidious and dark kind of Mage. Any of these options is possible, contrasting with the <i>Blood Treachery's</i> writers more or less saying &quot;Hello newly awakened Revenant Mage, nobody else will have you, so <a href=\"https://ibb.co/kHtZ297\" target=\"_blank\">these are</a> your <a href=\"https://ibb.co/6H2VvZn\" target=\"_blank\">new friends</a> .&quot; Joining the Nephandi is also possible, but it is certainly not a given.<br /> <br /> (I think it is also a disservice to the Nephandi to treat as simply the most evil group where persons who nobody else would want are dumped...but my more 'positive' interpretation of the Nephandi is another matter.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464268#post1464268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My guess would be the fact that Revenants generally tend towards monstrosity without being Mages. They're described as having a lesser Beast and often being violent and deranged. The majority becoming full-blown Nephandi is maybe a bit of a stretch, but half wouldn't surprise me in the least. It's not about the Nephandi swooping down on innocent little Revenant Mage children, but rather the natural tendencies of Revenants leading them in that direction. Arguably, the Curse of Caine might ping whatever they might detect in widderslaintes, but I had always thought widderslaintes just inevitably made their way back to the Nephandi on their own, not that they were actively recruited on a large scale, for much the same reason.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Book of Madness</i> 2nd edition has a paragraph about this. It is written there: &quot;<i>Nephandi are constantly on the lookout for latent Widderslainte, and will go to great lengths to bring them to fold.</i>&quot;<br /> Considering how very rare Widderslaintes are and how few in number (and pressed on many fronts) the Nephandi are, I think that there is no way other than some Magickal divination to explain the reliable recruitment. I cannot imagine Nephandi Mages sifting through all sorts of young malcontents and psychopaths looking for Widderslaintes, who might not be readily apparent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464351#post1464351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was a very silly Gygaxian &quot;no fun allowed&quot; rant in that book. Being a revenant mage (or worse - ghoul mage) is <i>far</i> from the powergaming choice when it comes to MtA. Not the worst thing you could do with your freebies, but not the best either. But misters Cohen and DiPessa seemed to think that it's something all the nasty minmaxers would drool over. Really strange, and I hope outdated, mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, a Revenant Mage does get some decent advantages (the ability to regenerate should also be noted), but definitely it is nothing to ring the powergamer alarm about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-19-2021, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T12:22:29-07:00","id":1464527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464522#post1464522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Book of Madness</i> 2nd edition has a paragraph about this. It is written there: &quot;<i>Nephandi are constantly on the lookout for latent Widderslainte, and will go to great lengths to bring them to fold.</i>&quot;<br /> Considering how very rare Widderslaintes are and how few in number (and pressed on many fronts) the Nephandi are, I think that there is no way other than some Magickal divination to explain the reliable recruitment. I cannot imagine Nephandi Mages sifting through all sorts of young malcontents and psychopaths looking for Widderslaintes, who might not be readily apparent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair nuff, that's why I acknowledged the possibility of Revenants pinging their widderslainte-senses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I haven't dug into the Nephandi too much yet, but I recalled reading that barrabi tend to envy widderslainte, which led me to guess that active recruiting is less common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T22:27:47-07:00","id":1464695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381250-was-blood-treachery-ever-even-mentioned-in-vampire?p=1464527#post1464527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair nuff, that's why I acknowledged the possibility of Revenants pinging their widderslainte-senses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I haven't dug into the Nephandi too much yet, but I recalled reading that barrabi tend to envy widderslainte, which led me to guess that active recruiting is less common.</div> </div> </div> </div>The information given about the Nephandi is relatively undeveloped, and often quite contradictory. Yes the Barrabi envy the Widderslainte and consider them to be too arrogant...yet at the same time the Widderslainte are more often than not the leaders of Nephandi Ahrimans. Though this one does make sense to an extent as some kind of twisted approach and outlook that the Nephandi would consider meaningful and worthwhile.<br /> <br /> I was just thinking about a Revenant Mage joining the Technocracy. A Revenant's experience and insights from being part of a Nightfolk group from birth (if Revenants could be called Nightfolk, considering that they are not one of the three main WoD splats) could give her or him some valuable unique perspectives. And wouldn't recruiting some Revenants be a clear and distinct proof that the Union can give all sorts of persons a place in their vision of the world? An Obertus in the NWO or a Grimaldi in the Syndicate do sound like cool and characterful archetypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-21-2021, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}